(5882342, 855361, 6388, '<td valign="top">the burning is a little obvious and the selective desaturation doesn''t add much for me, but aside from those things I like the image very much.  sharp and contrasty and all sorts of goodness.</td>', 'the burning is a little obvious and the selective desaturation doesn''t add much for me, but aside from those things I like the image very much.  sharp and contrasty and all sorts of goodness.', '2010-02-27 01:54:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(5882343, 854947, 6388, '<td valign="top">soft and pretty.  a bit Hallmark perhaps, but well executed.  the muted tones work nicely as well.</td>', 'soft and pretty.  a bit Hallmark perhaps, but well executed.  the muted tones work nicely as well.', '2010-02-27 01:55:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(5882344, 855520, 6388, '<td valign="top">i drank rum from a bottle that matched your shoes once.  the shallow depth works well and the technical details are good.  Either the white balance is a bit off or you''re getting a little fringing in the shadows (the blue under the toe) but it doesn''t detract from it really.  I wouldn''t mind if the crop were a little looser to add a little context, but all in all a solid entry.</td>', 'i drank rum from a bottle that matched your shoes once.  the shallow depth works well and the technical details are good.  Either the white balance is a bit off or you''re getting a little fringing in the shadows (the blue under the toe) but it doesn''t detract from it really.  I wouldn''t mind if the crop were a little looser to add a little context, but all in all a solid entry.', '2010-02-27 02:01:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(5882345, 854368, 6388, '<td valign="top">hmmmm, yes.  very nice.  i like the decision to focus on the bow and it''s nice and shallow to highlight that.  confident setup and well cropped.  I like it.</td>', 'hmmmm, yes.  very nice.  i like the decision to focus on the bow and it''s nice and shallow to highlight that.  confident setup and well cropped.  I like it.', '2010-02-27 02:02:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(5882346, 855384, 6388, '<td valign="top">some interesting elements to this.  not sure the exposed backlight adds anything to it, but i like the departure.  creative idea, good technical details, and well executed.</td>', 'some interesting elements to this.  not sure the exposed backlight adds anything to it, but i like the departure.  creative idea, good technical details, and well executed.', '2010-02-27 02:05:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(5882348, 855739, 6388, '<td valign="top">not sure the setup of the shoes works for me.  That said I suck at that kind of thing myself so I''d have no idea how to improve upon it.  Beyond that I think you nailed the effect I''m guessing you were going for - soft where it should be, sharp where it should be, well exposed with a nice vignette that draws me to the important parts of the photo.  I might have cropped a little of the right side to offset the slipper a bit, but that''s just a personal preference.  nice work</td>', 'not sure the setup of the shoes works for me.  That said I suck at that kind of thing myself so I''d have no idea how to improve upon it.  Beyond that I think you nailed the effect I''m guessing you were going for - soft where it should be, sharp where it should be, well exposed with a nice vignette that draws me to the important parts of the photo.  I might have cropped a little of the right side to offset the slipper a bit, but that''s just a personal preference.  nice work', '2010-02-27 02:11:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(5882349, 855447, 6388, '<td valign="top">hehe...very nice.  I like this image very much - the shoes are almost incidental, and i like that.  subtlety is often lost when the challenge topic is so literal.  Not gonna lie though...I''d have gone over the top happy if there were ripples in the water just beyond the dock :) (don''t get me wrong, I''m not suggesting you should have done that - it''s your photo, not mine - i just think that would have been hilarious).  nicely done.</td>', 'hehe...very nice.  I like this image very much - the shoes are almost incidental, and i like that.  subtlety is often lost when the challenge topic is so literal.  Not gonna lie though...I''d have gone over the top happy if there were ripples in the water just beyond the dock :) (don''t get me wrong, I''m not suggesting you should have done that - it''s your photo, not mine - i just think that would have been hilarious).  nicely done.', '2010-02-27 02:14:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(5882350, 855339, 6388, '<td valign="top">if you don''t count the concept, the composition, the unique square crop, the exposure, the muted tones, the sharpness, the post processing, and even the ridiculously perfect title, there''s absolutely nothing i like about this.<br/> <br/>my favourite so far.<br/> <br/>P</td>', 'if you don''t count the concept, the composition, the unique square crop, the exposure, the muted tones, the sharpness, the post processing, and even the ridiculously perfect title, there''s absolutely nothing i like about this. my favourite so far. P', '2010-02-27 02:22:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(5882351, 855668, 6388, '<td valign="top">great shoes.  not as big a fan of the colossal over-exposure slash high-key approach in this case.  I do like it from time to time, but in this case it eliminates all environmental context which makes me wonder what you''re hiding.  Just a personal preference - doesn''t mean i''m right or anything :)<br/> <br/>P</td>', 'great shoes.  not as big a fan of the colossal over-exposure slash high-key approach in this case.  I do like it from time to time, but in this case it eliminates all environmental context which makes me wonder what you''re hiding.  Just a personal preference - doesn''t mean i''m right or anything :) P', '2010-02-27 02:25:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(5882352, 854869, 6388, '<td valign="top">hate to be redundant, but i''m guessing you''ll get lots of comments on the border.  I''m not necessarily opposed to that style in the right circumstance - in this case it just seems to compete with the natural flow that the wire and the laces provide.  The concept is fun and the detail is good - absolutely love the mottled sky and cloud in the background.  should be an above average score</td>', 'hate to be redundant, but i''m guessing you''ll get lots of comments on the border.  I''m not necessarily opposed to that style in the right circumstance - in this case it just seems to compete with the natural flow that the wire and the laces provide.  The concept is fun and the detail is good - absolutely love the mottled sky and cloud in the background.  should be an above average score', '2010-02-27 02:29:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(5882353, 855742, 6388, '<td valign="top">oh so brave with selective desaturation AND motion blur all in one photo on DPC.  Maybe I''ve been away too long and voters accept this sort of thing now ;)<br/> <br/>I love the idea - the border is a bit overwhelming and I''d like to see the crop either more centred or more more off-centred. As it is it seems to me that the crop is a bit uncertain.  <br/> <br/>either way I applaud the departure from the ordinary and I enjoy the image for what it is.</td>', 'oh so brave with selective desaturation AND motion blur all in one photo on DPC.  Maybe I''ve been away too long and voters accept this sort of thing now ;) I love the idea - the border is a bit overwhelming and I''d like to see the crop either more centred or more more off-centred. As it is it seems to me that the crop is a bit uncertain.   either way I applaud the departure from the ordinary and I enjoy the image for what it is.', '2010-02-27 02:33:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(5882355, 855631, 6388, '<td valign="top">kind of cartoon-like and looking very processed...but for some reason i like it :)</td>', 'kind of cartoon-like and looking very processed...but for some reason i like it :)', '2010-02-27 02:39:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(5882357, 855838, 6388, '<td valign="top">oh Dave Hill I thank you for bringing this style to the mainstream.  the high-pass sharpen made some crazy halos on the right side and by the rear axle - actually not even sure anymore if you could fix that in the DPC ruleset.  Either way I don''t care because the overall effect is awesome.  Print it and frame it :)<br/> <br/>P</td>', 'oh Dave Hill I thank you for bringing this style to the mainstream.  the high-pass sharpen made some crazy halos on the right side and by the rear axle - actually not even sure anymore if you could fix that in the DPC ruleset.  Either way I don''t care because the overall effect is awesome.  Print it and frame it :) P', '2010-02-27 02:45:05.000000', NULL, 1),
